To achieve this, you can split the sentence into an array of words, reverse the order of adjectives within the array, and then join them back together. Here's a code snippet to do this:

```javascript
function switchAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(" ");
  const adjectives = words.filter(word => word.match(/^[a-zA-Z]+$/)); // filter out non-alphabetical words
  const reversedAdjectives = adjectives.reverse();
  const newSentence = reversedAdjectives.join(" ") + " " + words.filter(word => !word.match(/^[a-zA-Z]+$/)).join(" ");
  return newSentence;
}

const inputSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const outputSentence = switchAdjectives(inputSentence);
console.log(outputSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This function first splits the sentence into an array of words using `split()`. It then filters out any non-alphabetical words using a regular expression (`/^[a-zA-Z]+$/`). This is done to ensure that only the adjectives are reversed. Next, it reverses the order of the adjectives using `reverse()` and joins them back together using `join()`. Finally, it concatenates the reversed adjectives with the remaining words (which are not adjectives) and returns the new sentence.

